    {
      "text": "that they might raise up seed unto the Lord, 1 Ne. 7:1. prophet would the Lord God raise up among the Jews—even a Messiah, 1 Ne. 10:4. he raiseth up a righteous nation, 1 Ne. 17:37. Lord God will raise up a mighty nation among the Gentiles, 1 Ne. 22:7. God would raise up a righteous branch, 2 Ne. 3:5. choice seer will I raise up, 2 Ne. 3:7. Moses will I raise up, to deliver thy people, 2 Ne. 3:10. may God raise you from death, 2 Ne. 10:25. serpent which he did raise up before them, 2 Ne. 25:20. if I will … raise up seed unto me, Jacob 2:30. Lord … shall go forth … raising the dead, Mosiah 3:5. view this mortal body raised in immortality, Alma 5:15. all shall be raised from this temporal death, Alma 11:42. raised to an immortal body, Alma 11:45. resurrection, the raising of the spirit or the soul, Alma 40:15. mortality raised to immortality, Alma 41:4. taught … never to raise the sword, Alma 48:14. he did raise the standard of liberty, Alma 62:4. say unto this mountain—Be thou raised up, Hel. 12:17. his brother did he raise from the dead, 3 Ne. 7:19. whoso remembereth these sayings … will I raise up at the last day, 3 Ne. 15:1. they did heal the sick, and raise the dead, 4 Ne. 1:5. have hope … to be raised unto life eternal, Moro. 7:41.",
